MENTOR PROSE: Step 2 is about how hard each hammer hit turns the rock. Shake Control's Rotation expression gives each hit its own amount, rising from a quarter of a degree to half a degree to three quarters of a degree, and every hit settles at the same speed. The biggest turn I measured is about 0.6° at about 2.6 s, on the third hit. For step 2, open Shake Control's Rotation expression and look at those three amounts, then decide whether they match how hard you want each hit to land. Editing it isn't something I teach yet.
